statement:
Let $P$ and $P'$ be predicates on Boolean assignments, and let $q$ be a finite quantifier prefix, $	ext{ let }
\sigma$ a Boolean assignment, and $i$ a natural-number starting index. Suppose that $P$ and $P'$ agree on every assignment $	au$ that agrees with $	ext{ let }
\sigma$ at all indices below $i$. Then $q$ is true under $	ext{ let }
\sigma$ at index $i$ with predicate $P$ if and only if it is true there with predicate $P'$.
